{
  "id": "20812_zenin",
  "headword": "{是認|ぜにん}",
  "reading": "ぜにん",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "approval; acknowledgment; endorsement",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "approval; acknowledgment; endorsement",
      "explanation": "Formally recognizing something as correct, right, or acceptable. A written/formal word used in official, legal, and academic contexts."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "20812_zenin_ex1",
      "japanese": "その{行為|こうい}は{是認|ぜにん}できない。",
      "english": "That conduct cannot be approved.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20812_zenin_ex2",
      "japanese": "{委員会|いいんかい}が{計画|けいかく}を{是認|ぜにん}した。",
      "english": "The committee endorsed the plan.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20812_zenin_ex3",
      "japanese": "{暴力|ぼうりょく}を{是認|ぜにん}するような{発言|はつげん}は{厳|きび}しく{批判|ひはん}されるべきだ。",
      "english": "Statements that endorse violence should be severely criticized.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal word composed of {是|ぜ} (right/correct) and {認|にん} (acknowledge). Used in written language, official documents, and academic discourse. Implies deliberate judgment that something is acceptable or correct.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {是認|ぜにん}する: to approve/endorse\n- {是認|ぜにん}できない: unacceptable\n- {暗黙|あんもく}の{是認|ぜにん}: tacit approval\n- {是認|ぜにん}を{得|え}る: to obtain approval\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {承認|しょうにん}: approval — more common, used for official permission\n- {認可|にんか}: authorization — specifically granting a license or permit\n- {容認|ようにん}: tolerance/acceptance — accepting something even if not ideal",
